### Goal Model Decomposition

---

#### **Goal Table**

| Name       | Title                        | Text                                                                 | Runtime                         | Goal Type | Relation |
|------------|------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1         | Deliver Resources            | Deliver required resources from storage to the requesting agent's location. | `G2; G3` (sequential)           | Achieve   | AND      |
| G2         | Collect Resources            | Collect resources from storage locations in order of waiting time and path. | `FALLBACK(G4, G5)`              | Perform   | AND      |
| G3         | Deliver Resources            | Deliver collected resources to the requesting agent's location.          | `FALLBACK(G6, G7)`              | Perform   | AND      |
| G4         | Successful Collection        | Collect resources from all required storages in sequence.               | `G4.1; G4.2; G4.3; G4.4` (seq)  | Perform   | AND      |
| G5         | Battery Low During Collection| Return to recharging station and assign mission to another robot.       | `G5.1; G5.2` (sequential)       | Achieve   | OR       |
| G6         | Successful Delivery          | Deliver all collected resources to the requesting agent's location.     | `G6.1; G6.2` (sequential)       | Perform   | AND      |
| G7         | Battery Low During Delivery  | Return resource to checkpoint and assign remaining task to another robot. | `FALLBACK(G7.1, G8)`            | Achieve   | OR       |
| G8         | Alert for Delivery Failure   | Trigger alert and send report to sector manager if resource cannot be returned to checkpoint. | `-` (leaf)                      | Achieve   | AND      |

---

#### **Task Table**

| Name     | Title                        | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location        | Number of Robots |
|----------|------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------------|------------------|
| AT1      | Navigate to Storage          | Robot travels to the designated storage location.                   | G4.1     | Storage Facility | [1, N]           |
| AT2      | Request Resource             | Robot sends a message to the storage requesting specific resources. | G4.2     | Storage Facility | [1, N]           |
| AT3      | Wait for Resource Retrieval  | Robot waits until the requested resources are retrieved from storage. | G4.3     | Storage Facility | [1, N]           |
| AT4      | Return to Recharging Station | Robot returns to the recharging station due to low battery.         | G5.1     | Recharging Station | [1, N]           |
| AT5      | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Robot transfers the mission to another robot at the recharging station. | G5.2     | Recharging Station | [1, N]           |
| AT6      | Deliver Resource             | Robot transports the collected resource to the requesting agent's location. | G6.1     | Requesting Agent Location | [1, N]           |
| AT7      | Return Resource to Checkpoint | Robot returns the resource to a checkpoint due to low battery.       | G7.1     | Checkpoint       | [1, N]           |
| AT8      | Assign Remaining Task        | Robot transfers the remaining task to another robot at the checkpoint. | G7.2     | Checkpoint       | [1, N]           |
| AT9      | Trigger Alert                | Robot sends an alert and report to the sector manager.              | G8       | Checkpoint       | [1, N]           |

---

### **Logical Relationships**

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND][sequential]**  
  The mission requires both collecting and delivering resources.

- **G2 -> G4, G5 [OR][FALLBACK(G4, G5)]**  
  If the robot successfully collects resources (G4), the mission proceeds. If not (due to low battery), it transitions to G5.

- **G4 -> AT1, AT2, AT3 [AND][sequential]**  
  Collecting resources involves navigating to storage, requesting the resource, and waiting for retrieval.

- **G5 -> AT4, AT5 [AND][sequential]**  
  If the robot's battery is low during collection, it returns to the recharging station and assigns the mission to another robot.

- **G3 -> G6, G7 [OR][FALLBACK(G6, G7)]**  
  If delivery is successful (G6), the mission completes. If not (due to low battery), it transitions to G7.

- **G6 -> AT6 [AND][sequential]**  
  Delivery involves transporting resources to the requesting agent's location.

- **G7 -> G7.1, G8 [OR][FALLBACK(G7.1, G8)]**  
  If the robot can return the resource to a checkpoint (G7.1), it assigns the task to another robot. If not, it triggers an alert (G8).

- **G7.1 -> AT7, AT8 [AND][sequential]**  
  Returning the resource to a checkpoint involves transporting it and assigning the remaining task.

- **G8 -> AT9 [AND][sequential]**  
  Triggering an alert requires sending a report to the sector manager.

---

### **Summary**

- **Parallelism**: Multiple robots can be assigned to parallel `G4` (collection) and `G6` (delivery) tasks when multiple storages or resources are involved.
- **Fallbacks**: Battery-related failures (G5, G7) use fallback logic to ensure mission continuity.
- **Leaf Tasks**: AT1–AT9 represent actionable steps for robots, with locations and robot counts specified.
